WEBVTT

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:02.240
So moving to slide 10, Lectio.

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:09.200
So we had a strong quarter going, 59% driven by strong demand we saw across the globe. In the U.S.,

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:16.280
we were up 55% in quarter two. We outpaced the advanced lipid lowering market. This was driven

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:24.320
by monthly TRX growth of 49%, demonstrating Lectio's differentiated profile, strong

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:29.900
persistency. The demand is being driven with increasing depth in the priority health systems

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.320
that we're targeting. The most important segment,

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:36.660
yes, is this segment for us, which is the Medicare Part B segment,

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.480
where we see 23.3 percent share. That's up 3.6 percent year to date. And we see an

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:47.280
opportunity for a continued expansion. I think even with orals launching, our opportunity remains

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:53.320
for driving strong growth in the segments that wants infrequently administered physician-administered

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:58.080
medicines for light lipid lowering in the United States. And we see this as an

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.400
attractive and growing segment that supports our peak sales potential in the U.S.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:08.380
the U.S. and beyond. Outside of the U.S., NRDL inclusion is unlocking significant demand.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:14.160
We saw that in quarter one and continues in quarter two. Our market share has doubled now

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:21.420
versus the pre-NRDL share we were previously seeing. We also see sustained growth in Europe

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:26.460
and Japan, so overall pleased with our performance. We keep generating additional

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:33.800
data for Lectio. Three world studies demonstrated that Inclisir and Lectio improves adherence and

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.060
persistence compared to other advanced lipid-lowering therapies. And then we also have

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:43.760
the V-Challenge head-to-head study of Inclisirin versus mempidoic acid, which will prevent N-ESC.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:50.140
And lastly, we're on track as well for our two outcome studies to read out in 2027 for Lectio.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:56.140
Then moving to slide 11, Semblix had a very strong quarter, 89% constant

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:56.440
currency growth in the U.S. and in the U.S. and in the U.S. and in the U.S. and in the U.S.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:02.120
We see growth driven by both U.S. and ex-U.S. performance. In the U.S., we had 93%

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:07.640
growth in the quarter. This is driven by sustained leadership across all lines,

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.000
but importantly, we now expect to reach a first-line NBRX leadership share

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.800
in the second half of the year. You can see steady improvements in that NBRX share,

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:23.260
a first-line NBRX share. Outside of the U.S., we're primarily still driven by the third line

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:26.120
and beyond performance with 75%.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:34.100
But importantly, for future growth, we're seeing early-line adoption now starting to pick up.

